        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.782,
            0.104,
            0.9,
            0.121
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "MATHEMATICS"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.14,
            0.441,
            0.359
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We see from the table above that – 2, 0 and 2 are zeroes of the cubic polynomial "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x ^ { 3 } - 4 x ."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Observe that – 2, 0 and 2 are, in fact, the x-coordinates of the only points where the graph of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "y   =   x ^ { 3 }   -   4 x"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " intersects the x-axis. Since the curve meets the x-axis in only these 3 points, their x - coordinates are the only zeroes of the polynomial."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.366,
            0.44,
            0.475
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us take a few more examples. Consider the cubic polynomials "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x ^ { 3 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x ^ { 3 }   -   x ^ { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . We draw the graphs of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "y = x ^ { 3 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "y = x ^ { 3 } - x ^ { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " in Fig. 2.7 and Fig. 2.8 respectively."
            }
          ]
        },
